      "id": 62556,
      "name": "celette482",
      "username": "celette482",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/c/a5b964/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2013-05-05T11:51:35.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Thanks, everyone. It is a little OP, admittedly, but we promise to use it only in the direst of circumstances. We set up an entire game, had the counters out and everything- Akash-bhuta in Silver Gulch. I was playing Grandpa Legacy and Expat, and he had AA and Unity. Villian round had AA in ensnaring brambles and a carapace out. Luckily, the card is also irreducible.</p><p>I actually drew a hand and laid out my strategy. then he had my two best friends call and show up at my place, acting like they'd lost their minds (fake tattoos and mint juleps were involved) to distract me. When I came back up, he'd tucked another card into Legacy's hand.</p>",
